cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or build on this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Sudarshan: proof-carrying API security that survives the rewrite"
abstract: >-
  AI coding assistants rewrite applications wholesale, which silently invalidates
  route-pinned security regression tests and can drop authorization checks without
  any visible change. Sudarshan re-discovers moved API endpoints and re-proves
  broken object-level authorization against the current code using deterministic
  runtime evidence, with a three-state verdict that never reports an unproven
  application as safe. In a pre-registered benchmark of 25 synthetic route
  transformations, it detected 8 of 21 seeded regressions, reported 13 as
  inconclusive, and falsely cleared none (95% Wilson CI [0, 0.155]).
type: software
